- Concurrency means your program **can make progress on multiple tasks by switching between them**, even if only one CPU core is available.
- Parallelism means **multiple tasks are literally executing simultaneously**.
- Parallelism is typically considered a subset of concurrency.
- `GOMAXPROCS` controls how many OS threads can execute Go code simultaneously.
- GOMAXPROCS = 4 (4 tasks can be assigned to 4 OS threads)
